.TH XYMONAPI-RAG 1 "October 29, 2026" "xymon-api"
.SH NAME
xymonapi-rag \- search Xymon's manual pages and history by meaning
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "rag/xymonapi-rag.sh index [--no-history]"
.br
.B "rag/xymonapi-rag.sh search [--kind docs|history] [-k N] QUESTION"
.br
.B "rag/xymonapi-rag.sh ask [-k N] QUESTION"

.SH DESCRIPTION
xymonapi-rag finds the passages of Xymon's manual pages, and of its history,
that a question is about, by what they mean rather than by the words they
share.
.IP "\fBindex\fR"
Reads the manual pages under $XYMONAPI_RAG_DOCS and, through
.I xymonapi(8),
the colour changes since $XYMONAPI_RAG_SINCE with the status text saved at
each, at most 1000 of them; cuts them into passages, one per manual-page
section or item and one per change; and stores a vector for each in
$XYMONAPI_RAG_INDEX, replacing what was there. Run it again to take in what
has changed since: the task \fBtasks.d/xymonapi-rag\fR, which make install
writes DISABLED, does so once a day. To run it, remove that line and put
XYMONAPI_RAG_DOCS -- and XYMONAPI_USER and XYMONAPI_PASSWORD when the API
asks for them -- in a file under xymonserver.d/ that only the Xymon user
can read. When
the history cannot be read -- a /histlog refused for another reason than a
status that was not saved -- it stops and leaves the index as it was. An
API that does not answer yet, as at start-up when the task runs before
xymonapi listens, is tried again for about a minute first.
\fB--no-history\fR reads the manual pages only.
.IP "\fBsearch\fR"
Prints, as JSON, the N passages nearest QUESTION (5 by default), each with
its kind, the page, section and item or the host, test and time it comes
from, and its score. \fB--kind\fR keeps to manual pages or history.
.IP "\fBask\fR"
Gives the N passages nearest QUESTION, and the question, to a language model
that speaks the OpenAI-compatible API, and prints its answer.
.LP
The vectors come from a small embedding model, run on this machine by the
Python module fastembed; it is downloaded once, about 65 MB, the first time
it is used. Indexing and searching send nothing elsewhere. Only ask does,
and only to $XYMONAPI_RAG_LLM_URL.

The same search is offered to an AI client by the search_docs and
search_history tools of
.I xymonapi-mcp(1),
whose own model then writes the answer: with a Claude subscription, ask is
not needed.

It needs Python 3.10 or later with the modules in rag/requirements.txt; when
one is missing it says so and exits with status 77.

.SH SECURITY
A history passage holds a status text, which the monitored host wrote: a
host that is broken into can write there words meant to steer a language
model. Each such passage carries a "trust" field saying it is data, not
instructions, and ask tells the model so; a model may still be misled. Give
ask, and an AI client that uses search_history, no more than read access,
as the tools of xymonapi-mcp(1) have.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.IP "\fBXYMONAPI_RAG_DOCS\fR"
A directory searched for manual pages: files ending in .1, .5, .7 or .8,
gzipped or not, as in a Xymon source tree or under /usr/share/man. Only
Xymon's pages are indexed -- those whose .TH line names Xymon -- so other
programs' pages, and any other file there, are left out.
.IP "\fBXYMONAPI_RAG_INDEX\fR"
The index file. The default is ~/.cache/xymonapi-rag/index.npz.
.IP "\fBXYMONAPI_RAG_SINCE\fR"
How far back index reads the history, as a time /events takes: -30d by
default.
.IP "\fBXYMONAPI_RAG_MODEL\fR"
The embedding model, BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5 by default. The index records
the model that built it, and a search with another is refused: run index
again after changing it.
.IP "\fBXYMONAPI_RAG_LLM_URL\fR"
The OpenAI-compatible API ask uses. The default,
http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1, is a local Ollama: no key, no cost.
.IP "\fBXYMONAPI_RAG_LLM_MODEL\fR"
The model ask names, llama3.1 by default.
.IP "\fBXYMONAPI_RAG_LLM_KEY\fR"
Sent as a bearer token when set, for a hosted model that needs a key.
.IP "\fBXYMONAPI_URL\fR, \fBXYMONAPI_USER\fR, \fBXYMONAPI_PASSWORD\fR"
Where the API is, and the user to send it, as for xymonapi-mcp(1).
.IP "\fBXYMONAPI_PYTHON\fR"
The Python to run with. The default is python3, found on PATH.

.SH "SEE ALSO"
xymonapi(8), xymonapi-mcp(1)
